{"mappings":[{"caseId":"HEART-004","rationale":"The all, latest and skip subtests evaluate at base+35 with a 10-second recurrence and MaxBatch=2. All asserts two work occurrences after one evaluation and four after a second at the same time, supporting bounded batches and retained backlog. Latest asserts nominal=base+30 and covered_count=4. Skip asserts one skipped work occurrence. Limits: skip does not check which nominal instants are recorded as omitted; all does not inspect individual identities or coverage; no actual downtime/restart is exercised. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestCatchUp"},{"caseId":"HEART-006","rationale":"The test attempts and acknowledges an occurrence, closes and reopens the store, and checks that serialized status contains acknowledged and contains no verified state. Evaluating at base+21 must create exactly one return-review occurrence, supporting preservation of unresolved acknowledgement and a return watch across restart. Limits: acknowledgement is invoked directly without transport; status is checked by string matching; the test does not directly inspect the persisted deadline or assert an explicit possibly-executed classification. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestUncertainEffectAndRestartQuestions"}]}
